<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela may out-source $215 mln dam project.</title>
<headline>Venezuela may out-source $215 mln dam project.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela is considering opening the final stages of a $215 million hydro-electric dam project at Uribante-Caparo in the mountainous western state of Tachira to private investment, the Finance Ministry said.</p>
<p>Potential investors will be able to bid at an auction planned for the beginning of December, the Ministry said in a press statement quoting state-owned electricity company Cadafe.</p>
<p>The project has already absorbed some $2.86 billion in investment. On completion, it will generate over 300 megawatts of electricity, the release added.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
